        "id": "s1_lake",
        "kind": "text",
        "label": "The lake ecosystem",
        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Identity",
        "lines": [
          "Lakes are large inland water bodies that",
          "contain still water, and they hold water",
          "throughout the year.",
          "A lake ecosystem performs all the functions",
          "of an ecosystem: photosynthesis,",
          "heterotrophs feeding on autotrophs,",
          "decomposition, mineralization, recycling of",
          "minerals and circulation of nutrients.",
          "A deep water lake has three distinct zones:",
          "1) Littoral zone  2) Limnetic zone",
          "3) Profundal zone"
        ],
        "why": "The three zone names in order from the shore outwards and downwards are the plan of the whole answer, so they are written before anything is described and every later part is filed under one of them.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Describing a lake only as a body of water. The answer must say it is a complete ecosystem.",
          "Naming the zones in the wrong order. Littoral is at the shore, limnetic is the open middle, profundal is the deep bottom."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Three zones, from the edge inwards and then downwards: littoral, limnetic, profundal.",
        "margin_note": "One line on what a lake is, one on the functions, then the three names. Do not describe the zones yet."
